From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 02:32:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 185/185] Sega CD: acknowledge each on-screen-keyboard scancode

GA_KEY is a single latest-wins word. The servant posts one scancode per
frame and this handler reads one per INT2, and the assumption that
those rates never slip held until a serial keyboard could type during a
redraw: two posts between two reads is one latch, and the earlier
scancode is gone before it was seen. Measured on the scripted serial
rig -- "hello world" arrived with letters missing and their Enters
intact, which is also exactly what the Flipper Zero produced on real
hardware.

The COMFLG sub byte has been dead since the SP finished the boot
handshake, so it becomes the acknowledgement: the seq of each processed
scancode is echoed there, and the servant holds its queue until the
echo matches. The on-screen keyboard's own presses are unaffected.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 776df61..93a9fa1 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -4249,6 +4249,24 @@ void segacd_int_2_c(void)
                 call_ikbdraw(sc);
                 call_ikbdraw((UBYTE)(sc | 0x80));
             }
+            /* Acknowledge, so the servant may post the next one.
+             *
+             * GA_KEY is a single latest-wins word, and the assumption
+             * that one post per frame meets one INT2 per frame held
+             * right up until a serial keyboard could type during a
+             * redraw: an interrupt arriving while the previous one is
+             * still being serviced is latched, two arriving are still
+             * one latch, and the earlier scancode is gone before it
+             * was ever read. Measured, not supposed: "hello world"
+             * through the scripted serial rig arrived as nine letters,
+             * with the two that shared a frame with a long redraw
+             * missing and their Enters intact.
+             *
+             * The COMFLG sub byte has been dead since the SP finished
+             * the boot handshake, which makes it the one free channel
+             * back: the servant now holds its queue until the seq it
+             * posted comes back through here. */
+            *(volatile UBYTE *)0xFF800F = seq;
         }
     }
 
